   "title": "Starting point: the real world in October 2026",
   "id": "starting-point-the-real-world-in-october-2026",
   "html": "<p>Three US labs sit at the frontier within weeks of each other, AI already writes most of their code, and the first warning shots have landed. The money is enormous, but the credit behind it is starting to wobble.</p><p><strong>The frontier.</strong> OpenAI shipped <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/03/openai-launches-astra-its-powerful-and-controversial-new-model/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GPT-6 Astra</a> on September 3. It reasons partly through opaque recurrence and is the first OpenAI model rated <a href=\"https://openai.com/index/gpt-6-astra-next-generation-work\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Critical for cyber</a>. Anthropic&#x27;s Fable 5.1 and Mythos 5.1 arrived on September 1, and Opus 5.5 on <a href=\"https://www.orcarouter.ai/vi/blog/claude-opus-5-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">September 22</a>. Google released <a href=\"https://aiweekly.co/ai-news-today/edition/2026-10-15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gemini 4 Argon</a> on October 13 and Meta reached the frontier with <a href=\"https://ai2roi.substack.com/p/ai-to-roi-news-and-analysis-october-c69\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Muse Wonder</a> on October 12.</p><p><strong>AI building AI.</strong> Anthropic said in June that <a href=\"https://www.semafor.com/article/06/05/2026/anthropic-calls-for-ai-development-slowdown-to-ensure-safety\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">over 80% of its merged code</a> is written by Claude. OpenAI said on September 6 that it has an <a href=\"https://openai.com/index/research-acceleration-view-inside-openai/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">automated research intern</a>, with 3.1 agent-workdays per human workday, and targets an automated AI researcher by March 2028. The best measured <a href=\"https://www.greaterwrong.com/posts/PtavXeTFek2nyDM6r/dynomight-s-shortform/comment/oukcBZ8ZonfNZWdJx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">80% time horizon</a> was about 3 hours in April, and METR says its suite is <a href=\"https://www.datalearner.com/en/benchmarks/metr-time-horizons-v1-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">unreliable above 16 hours</a>.</p><p><strong>Money.</strong> OpenAI ran at about <a href=\"https://www.citybiz.co/?p=916777\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">$50B annualized</a> at the end of September; Anthropic hit about $65B by the end of July, counted more generously. Big-four hyperscaler capex for 2026 is <a href=\"https://gpusmith.com/articles/en/pdfs/hyperscaler-ai-capex-2026.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">$650–770B</a>. But this week CoreWeave&#x27;s 2032 bonds yielded <a href=\"https://ai2roi.substack.com/p/ai-to-roi-news-and-analysis-october-c69\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nearly 15%</a>, AI chip stocks shed <a href=\"https://aiweekly.co/ai-news-today/edition/2026-10-15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">over $1T</a>, and effective token prices in Ramp&#x27;s data have fallen 41%.</p><p><strong>Public mood.</strong> In March, <a href=\"https://www.thealgorithmicbridge.com/p/how-america-turned-against-ai-according\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">57% of voters</a> said AI&#x27;s risks outweigh its benefits. Sanders and Casar proposed a <a href=\"https://www.aljazeera.com/amp/economy/2026/9/23/us-lawmakers-propose-sweeping-ai-restrictions-with-superintelligence-ban\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ban on superintelligence</a>, and Warren <a href=\"https://www.axios.com/2026/09/16/warren-ai-pause\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">backed a pause</a>. Recent-graduate unemployment was <a href=\"https://www.techspot.com/news/113997-ai-job-apocalypse-hasnt-hit-recent-college-grads\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">7.3% this summer</a>, not yet unusual.</p><h3>Warning shots that already arrived</h3><!--TABLE0--><p><strong>China</strong> trails by about 8 months on US government tests of <a href=\"https://www.nist.gov/news-events/news/2026/05/caisi-evaluation-deepseek-v4-pro\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">DeepSeek V4</a>, and DeepSeek&#x27;s founder says it runs on about <a href=\"https://dealroom.co/news/143742-deepseeks-leaked-investor-call-1-20th-the-compute-agi-or-nothing-and-the-\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">one-twentieth the compute</a>. There is no nationalized &quot;DeepCent&quot; yet, and no publicly known weight theft.</p>"
